  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRA Sudan Crisis 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Even before the ongoing famine crisis, Sudan had 3.7 million displaced people in the country with dire humanitarian needs. The fighting between the Sudan Armed Forces (SAF) and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF) on multiple fronts have resulted in massive displacement, civilian deaths and injuries, and loss of livelihoods amid deteriorating economic conditions. The conflict has a substantial impact on the country&#x2019;s food system and hinders people&#x2019;s ability to cope with food shortages. Potentially the world&#x2019;s worst hunger crisis could be observed in Sudan with already 18 million people acutely food insecure, up from 9 million in 2022. The latest IPC report highlights that 8.5 million people are experiencing extreme food shortages, and catastrophic hunger conditions, while 755,000 people face imminent famine.The Joint Response aims to contribute to available of, access to and consumption of food in Darfur. The activities  include vouchers, cash assistance, and in-kind support.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Save the Children (SC) &amp; CDF will provide FSL &amp; nutrition support in Rokoro (in Central Darfur) with the  aim of restoring livelihood activities, improving food access and reducing mortality &amp; morbidity rates. This project will expand SC&#x2019;s &amp; CDF&#x2019;s current food security response and is built upon successful  modalities implemented by WFP &amp; Federal Ministry of Health. 60 host community HHs will receive a one-off cash support of USD70 for seeds &amp; agricultural tools for their kitchen garden, which can still be cultivated during rainy season, based on guidelines from FSL cluster. These HHs will also be provided with agricultural training &amp; technical support. In addition, 242 IDP HHs will receive 3 tranches of cash for food (158USD) based on WFP guidelines. Cash support will encourage local procurement and cash for seeds &amp; tools will increase overall availability of food. Besides, the cash &amp; nutrition response will be supplemented with hygiene promotion, cooking demonstrations and social behavior change communication (SBCC) on IYCF to improve nutrition outcomes. Protection will be mainstreamed through awareness raising on GBV, CP and MHPSS. Referral to SC&#x2019;s and other actors&#x2019; WASH, health, SRH &amp; vaccination programs will be provided, e.g. to SC&#x2019;s &amp; MSF&#x2019;s health facilities and mobile clinics.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support the most vulnerable people in Rokoro.  SC&#x2019;s needs assessment found that children, elderly, women, PwD and PLW are most in need.</narrative>
  </description>
